+  "requirements": "Network access for registry specs, or one or two packed @pmndrs/glyph .tgz artifacts. Never builds workspace source. --saved-candidate <report-directory> reuses an exact artifact's saved candidate instead of timing it again, with matching environment and sampling checks. Accepts --suite smoke|layout|measure|glyphs|publication|spans|batch|style|reflow|stress|cold|edit|assignment|edit-sized|multi-owner|bulk-1024-profile|frontier|full. --sampling adaptive|single-call defaults to adaptive; --warmup conditional|fixed-20 defaults to conditional. Use --sampling single-call --warmup fixed-20 uniformly for a fixed-warmup comparison. Full baselines require all 145 candidate identities unless --baseline-availability published-no-outlines explicitly permits the two documented outline omissions. Optional candidate-only diagnostic profiling requires both --profile-tag <@tag> and --cpu-profile-output <directory>; it selects that Labs tag and cannot be combined with --baseline or --saved-candidate. Profiled timings are diagnostic and are not a normal performance comparison.",
   "writes": "Ignored Labs results, an artifact manifest, and a Markdown summary.md (also appended to $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY when set) under --output (default .cache/labs-package); optional V8 CPU profiles are written under --cpu-profile-output."
